400,67,3,387,6785,1931,5109,1741,429,400,18,21,64,488,220,19,65,488,220,19,66,488,220,18,67,284,220,17,20,2418,220,7379,279,7192,897,315,198,78045,64,1124,15136,1124,26888,90,65,92,1124,15136,1124,26888,58,18,15370,66,92,1124,15136,1124,26888,58,19,15370,67,92,7110,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nLet $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ and $d$ be positive real numbers such that $36a + 4b + 4c + 3d = 25.$  Find the maximum value of\n\\[a \\times \\sqrt{b} \\times \\sqrt[3]{c} \\times \\sqrt[4]{d}.\\]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"2de17349d2d1c86b044b03c314cdb17fa7aaf2bf8b169f36bc351ecf136830e7"},"seconds":89.38662075996399,"seed":969490349224390067,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the maximum value of the expression \\(a \\times \\sqrt{b} \\times \\sqrt[3]{c} \\times \\sqrt[4]{d}\\) under the constraint \\(36a + 4b + 4c + 3d = 25\\), we can use the method of Lagrange multipliers or apply the AM-GM inequality for simplicity.\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the expression to apply the AM-GM inequality effectively:\n\\[a \\times \\sqrt{b} \\times \\sqrt[3]{c} \\times \\sqrt[4]{d}.\\]\n\nWe need to balance the terms in the constraint \\(36a + 4b + 4c + 3d = 25\\) with the terms in the expression. To do this, we can use the AM-GM inequality on the terms \\(36a, 4b, 4c, 3d\\).\n\nBy AM-GM inequality, we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{36a + 4b + 4c + 3d}{4} \\geq \\sqrt[4]{36a \\cdot 4b \\cdot 4c \\cdot 3d}.\n\\]\nGiven that \\(36a + 4b + 4c + 3d = 25\\), we substitute this into the inequality:\n\\[\n\\frac{25}{4} \\geq \\sqrt[4]{36a \\cdot 4b \\cdot 4c \\cdot 3d}.\n\\]\nRaising both sides to the fourth power, we get:\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{25}{4}\\right)^4 \\geq 36a \\cdot 4b \\cdot 4c \\cdot 3d.\n\\]\nSimplifying the left side, we have:\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{25}{4}\\right)^4 = \\frac{25^4}{4^4} = \\frac{390625}{256}.\n\\]\nSo,\n\\[\n\\frac{390625}{256} \\geq 36a \\cdot 4b \\cdot 4c \\cdot 3d = 576abcd.\n\\]\nThus,\n\\[\nabcd \\leq \\frac{390625}{256 \\cdot 576} = \\frac{390625}{147456}.\n\\]\nNow, we need to find the value of \\(a \\times \\sqrt{b} \\times \\sqrt[3]{c} \\times \\sqrt[4]{d}\\). To achieve equality in the AM-GM inequality, we need \\(36a = 4b = 4c = 3d\\). Let \\(36a = 4b = 4c = 3d = k\\). Then we have:\n\\[\n36a = k \\implies a = \\frac{k}{36},\n\\]\n\\[\n4b = k \\implies b = \\frac{k}{4},\n\\]\n\\[\n4c = k \\implies c = \\frac{k}{4},\n\\]\n\\[\n3d = k \\implies d = \\frac{k}{3}.\n\\]\nSubstituting these into the constraint, we get:\n\\[\n36a + 4b + 4c + 3d = k + k + k + k = 4k = 25 \\implies k = \\frac{25}{4}.\n\\]\nSo,\n\\[\na = \\frac{k}{36} = \\frac{25}{4 \\cdot 36} = \\frac{25}{144},\n\\]\n\\[\nb = \\frac{k}{4} = \\frac{25}{4 \\cdot 4} = \\frac{25}{16},\n\\]\n\\[\nc = \\frac{k}{4} = \\frac{25}{16},\n\\]\n\\[\nd = \\frac{k}{3} = \\frac{25}{4 \\cdot 3} = \\frac{25}{12}.\n\\]\nNow, we calculate the expression:\n\\[\na \\times \\sqrt{b} \\times \\sqrt[3]{c} \\times \\sqrt[4]{d} = \\frac{25}{144} \\times \\sqrt{\\frac{25}{16}} \\times \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{25}{16}} \\times \\sqrt[4]{\\frac{25}{12}}.\n\\]\nSimplifying each term, we get:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\frac{25}{16}} = \\frac{5}{4},\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{25}{16}} = \\frac{\\sqrt[3]{25}}{2},\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sqrt[4]{\\frac{25}{12}} = \\frac{\\sqrt[4]{25}}{\\sqrt[4]{12}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt[4]{12}}.\n\\]\nSo the expression becomes:\n\\[\n\\frac{25}{144} \\times \\frac{5}{4} \\times \\frac{\\sqrt[3]{25}}{2} \\times \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt[4]{12}} = \\frac{25 \\cdot 5 \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{25} \\cdot \\sqrt{5}}{144 \\cdot 4 \\cdot 2 \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{12}} = \\frac{125 \\sqrt[6]{25^3} \\sqrt{5}}{1152 \\sqrt[4]{12}} = \\frac{125 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 5^{1/2}}{1152 \\cdot 12^{1/4}} = \\frac{625 \\cdot 5^{1/2}}{1152 \\cdot 12^{1/4}}.\n\\]\nSimplifying further, we find that:\n\\[\na \\times \\sqrt{b} \\times \\sqrt[3]{c} \\times \\sqrt[4]{d} = \\frac{125}{144}.\n\\]\nThus, the maximum value is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{125}{144}}.\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{125}{144}}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
